   &+LRising nearly two-hundred feet into the air, this &+ytree &+Lhas a distinctive and
unique multi-hued &+ybark&+L. Stretches of outer &+ybark &+Lfall away at periodically over
the course of the year, revealing a bright lime-green inner &+Gbark&+L. With time,
this patch darkens and matures from &+Cblue &+Lto &+Mpurple&+L, then &+yorange&+L, and finally to
&+rre&+md&+rd&+mis&+rh-ma&+mr&+ro&+mon &+Ltones. In the north, the &+ytree &+Lis known as a rainbow &+ceu&+yc&+ca&+yly&+cp&+yt&+cus
&+Lbecause of its colorful display. Being the only specimen of the &+ytree &+Lin this
&+Gfo&+gr&+Ge&+gst&+L, the &+Gpygmies &+Lhave come to consider it the heart of their tribe. Over
the years, the tribal &+gelders &+Lhave taken to holding their &+wcouncil &+Lunder its
shade.
~
